  "short_description": "Logical Observation Identifiers Names and Codes \u2014 100,000+ lab & clinical observation codes. Free download after registration at loinc.org. Load data via: flask forge templates install-data loinc",
  "long_description": "LOINC (Logical Observation Identifiers Names and Codes) provides 100,000+ universal codes for laboratory and clinical observations \u2014 from blood glucose measurements to radiology reports. The schema includes the main code table, hierarchical classification tree, multilingual variants, and answer list definitions for coded observations. Data download is free after registration at loinc.org.",
  "when_to_use": "Use alongside FHIR R4 for any lab, pathology, or clinical measurement system. Required by CMS in the US for electronic lab reporting. Essential when storing structured clinical results that must be understood by multiple systems without proprietary code translation."
